    "nodes": {
      "1": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "1/X\nThis node divides 1 by the incoming value. This is a quick way to proportionally inverse a signal.\nIn this example the green circle is inversely proportional to the size of the other circle. The bigger the other gets, the smaller this gets and vice versa\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n• The Sine modulates the radii of the two rings. The red ring is modulated directly by the Sine, the green ring is modulated by the proportionally inverse of the signal."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 195.77487182617188,
          "width": 755.8348388671875,
          "x": 107.58299255371094,
          "y": 196.28021240234375
        },
        "class": {
